The function iterates over each string in the input list. Each string is split into words using whitespace as the delimiter. For each word, we check if its first character (converted to lowercase) equals `'p'`. If it does, we add it to a temporary result list. Once we collect two such words, we immediately return them as a tuple. This ensures we pick the first two words starting with 'p' encountered in the order they appear.

